## Part 6 — Reviewer Focus Guide

Tell the human reviewer exactly where to spend their time:

```
REVIEW THESE FIRST (High risk):
  → core/auth.py lines 108–115 (auth logic changed)
  → payments/client.py lines 40–55 (new external call)

SPOT CHECK THESE (Medium risk):
  → utils/helpers.py lines 200–210 (new function, no test)

SKIP DETAILED REVIEW (Low risk):
  → tests/tools/test_slack.py (test file only)
  → README.md (docs only)
```

---

## Part 7 — Self-Check

Before emitting:
- [ ] Every flag cites exact file:line from the diff
- [ ] Blast radius assessment based on actual import evidence, not guessing
- [ ] Score arithmetic is shown
- [ ] Hallucination check performed (all called functions verified against repo)
- [ ] "Safe to merge" recommendation is explicit

